{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And Sarah died.</b> The verse alludes, in its saying <b>in Kiryat Arba</b>, to say that, heaven forbid, death is not attributed to the righteous; rather, Kiryat Arba means a city built of four elements — she was separate from them and departed from them. And its saying <b>the same is Hebron</b> means that even though she died, she still exerted upon them an aspect of joining (ḥibbur), for the righteous, even though their body dies, are not deprived of life, since the righteous in their death are called alive. Go and learn (Shabbat 152b) from the incident of Rav Aḥa bar Yoshiya. And the reason is that while they are in this world, they transform the aspect of materiality within the elements into the aspect of holy spirituality that is in the soul, by means of good deeds and the intensification of Torah [study] that they exert themselves in in this world. And to give you understanding in this matter, go and learn what Rambam wrote, chapter 4 of Hilkhot Yesodei HaTorah, the law of the four elements: that one element can change into the nature of its fellow element nearest to it, and dust can turn into water. And likewise one finds that by means of a person's cleaving to his Creator, all the elements transform into the element of fire, and the element of fire into the element of the fire of the soul — and understand." "And its saying <b>in the land of Canaan</b>: for this world is called ״the land of Canaan״ (Zohar vol. I, p. 80) — it is the evil inclination, and by means of strengthening against it, a person can attain to act wondrously in holiness and in spiritual attainment." "<b>To mourn for Sarah and to weep for her.</b> Meaning: for Sarah, who died from the world; and to weep for her, on account of what is lacking because of her absence. Or it may say the reverse — <b>for Sarah</b>, on account of her righteousness and what is lacking because of her absence; <b>and to weep for her</b>, on account of what touches her [herself], that she tasted the cup of death and her sun set."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:42:51.111222995Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}